  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which D-Cysteine may interact with the Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit, through a series of target interactions involving riboflavin synthase. D-Cysteine is directly linked to riboflavin synthase, which is a target of both Saniculamoid D and Hemiasterlin, both of which are implicated in targeting the Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit. This indicates that D-Cysteine may act as a modulator of the riboflavin synthase pathway, potentially influencing the structural integrity of the hemagglutinin protein. The consistent presence of D-Cysteine as a target of riboflavin synthase across multiple paths supports a plausible mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence suggests that D-Cysteine could exert its effects through a pathway involving riboflavin synthase, which in turn may affect the hemagglutinin subunit, though further experimental validation is required to confirm this relationship.",
